    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 8 slate with a heavy emphasis on elite sprint speed and favorable platoon matchups. Our strongest play is **Christian Yelich** (74.33), who benefits significantly from an advantageous R/R platoon split and a prime #1 lineup spot against McGreevy. Right behind him, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.03) is a must-start; despite a challenging matchup against a strong arm in Kremer, the projected +16% park factor boost and his elite speed profile make him an essential engine for our stolen base targets today. Conversely, **Josh Smith** (64.66) and **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) are anchored by dynamic platoon edges, with **Josh Smith**\u2019s #2 order position providing a high-floor opportunity to accumulate counting stats.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Chase Meidroth** (50.55), who remained the closest cut from the active lineup. While **Chase Meidroth** offered a respectable efficiency score, the optimizer favored the higher ceilings of **Colt Keith** (60.34) and **Luke Raley** (59.62) due to superior park factors and more favorable platoon splits. We must monitor the official lineups closely, as **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Trea Turner**, **Colt Keith**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** are all currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Furthermore, while **Junior Caminero** (63.19) is a strong utility option, facing Gerrit Cole introduces volatility, though his current form keeps him comfortably ahead of lower-tier bench bats like **Pedro Ramirez** and **Casey Schmitt**. Proceed with caution regarding the potential for late-game defensive substitutions or weather-related delays given the sensitivity of our core speed contributors.",
